# Company logo artwork, and the images that contain it, stays out of the
# public repository. The live site serves the real files. On a fresh clone
# these spots simply appear blank, which the README notes is expected.
www/interstate/assets/interstate-logo.webp
www/interstate/favicon.png
www/seedtoseed/assets/seedtoseed.svg
www/interstate/assets/og-interstate.webp
www/interstate/assets/og-interstate.jpg
www/seedtoseed/assets/og-seedtoseed.webp
www/seedtoseed/assets/og-seedtoseed.jpg

# Sunnyvale Jenn's logo is the only artwork held back from her experience.
# The 3D room never reproduces the mark, it only borrows the teals, so
# og-sunnyvalejenn.* is an ordinary scene capture and ships.
www/sunnyvalejenn/assets/svj-1.webp
www/sunnyvalejenn/assets/svj-1.jpg

# John Walker's likeness, and only that. His photographs, and poster.webp,
# which is his own printed flyer and carries his photograph, his phone
# number, and his email address.
#
# HIS W IS NOT ON THIS LIST, on purpose, and neither is the social card the
# W sits on. The path data is inline in www/automan/index.html twice, because
# the mark is the intro panel's bullet and the info button's glyph rather than
# a loaded image, so no rule here can hold the shape back. Once that is true,
# withholding favicon.svg only costs the tab icon and the loading screen on a
# fresh clone, and withholding og-automan.* only costs the SHARE preview its
# image (the home page card is a different file, card-automan.webp, a render
# of the showroom rather than the mark), while og-card.html and
# css/og-card.css ship the recipe that regenerates it from favicon.svg
# anyway. None of that protects anything.
#
# So the mark ships and stays John's: our MIT license covers the code that
# draws it and not the mark itself. That carve-out is stated in LICENSE, in
# README.md, in www/terms.html, in the comment at the top of favicon.svg, and
# beside the inline paths in index.html. The line this list draws is likeness,
# which cannot be regenerated from anything here.
www/automan/assets/john-walker-about.webp
www/automan/assets/john-walker-avatar.webp
www/automan/assets/john-walker-profile.webp
www/automan/assets/poster.webp
